  "notes": "Atlanta contralto across the Dupri / Soulshock / Darkchild board, 1995–2003. The research reads \"61–109 straight; ballads 61–85\", so the straight band 85–109 is the base with the mode at 92 (the sourced \"Angel of Mine\" reading) and `halfTime` false; the entry's note that \"ballads move the snare to beat 3 of a doubled grid\" is the other backbeat class and is not folded in here. Three drum deltas: \"soft-attack programmed kit\" with the kick at two or three hits a bar and the genre's syncopation halved, \"hand-claps layered on 2&4\" as a clap stack with a tight offset, and \"16th hats at low velocity\" — continuous, but at a main-velocity floor of 0.34 against the genre's 0.8. Harmony is \"two-chord minor-9th vamps, Rhodes and string pad\", so the ninth share climbs to 0.4 and the families stay two-chord; \"a guitar or harp figure as the recognisable lick\" is the counter with `answer_lick` and `arp` sharing weight. \"Her low-alto placement forces keys with a comfortable 4th–5th above the tonic\" is why the melody register is the lowest of the batch's soloists and the interval spread is narrow. ⚠ Confidence is medium — the research says \"one fully sourced song plus a tempo spine\" — and it marks the bass's slide and the bridge whole-step lift `[LOW-CONF]`; the slide is carried as a 0.3 `glideProb` and the modulation has no field, so it is recorded here only. ⚠ The other INFERRED parameters are all velocity and density numbers and `swing.amount` 0.54. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `C#m`, and the remaining values `Fm`, `Gm`, `Bbm`, together with all 4 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
